description:
FILED s536b (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-08) from the #4561 / #4562 board acceptance (Role-Tiny concrete-methods.t, which runs to its plan since s536b: 5 of 7).

REPRODUCER (scratch/s536b/p/s2.pl in the s536b worktree; perl 5.40.3):

    BEGIN {
      package P;
      sub st; sub st2 ($); sub real { 1 }
      BEGIN { print "1 ", join(",", sort grep !/::$/, keys %P::), "\n" }
      sub later;
    }
    package Q; sub qs;
    BEGIN { print "2 ", join(",", sort grep !/::$/, keys %Q::), "\n" }
    sub ql;

perl: `1 BEGIN,real,st,st2` / `2 BEGIN,qs` (`later` and `ql` are not there yet).  PCL (s536b tree): `1 later,real,st,st2` / `2 ql,qs`.  (`BEGIN` itself is a separate, known difference.)

MECHANISM: s536b (#4561) made a bodyless `sub NAME;` a stash entry -- `(p-declare-sub pl-NAME :forward)` records it for p-stash.  But that form is emitted into the section's DECLARATIONS bucket (Parser.pm _process_sub_statement unshift, Parser2.pm 2478 @decls, _lower_named_sub_stmt's _hoisted_decls), which loads before every BEGIN / `use` of the section; perl creates the stub CV when the compiler REACHES the declaration, in source order with BEGIN and use.  Before s536b no forward declaration was visible at all (the view hid every stub), so this is the other side of the same fact.
Effect: Role::Tiny records a role's subs at `use Role::Tiny` (import) as non-methods; with every stub already present -- and since s536b `\&stub == \&stub` (one late-bound ref per name) -- `after_stub` / `after_stub_proto`, declared AFTER the import, compare equal and are dropped from the method list: concrete-methods.t row 1 ("only subs after Role::Tiny import are methods") and row 3 ("methods_provided_by gives method list") fail.
FIX SHAPE (not built): split the :forward form -- the stub creation stays at the section head (calls and `\&foo` written above the declaration must still resolve), and the stash-view record (the `*p-forward-subs*` entry, perhaps the :stub status for `exists &foo` too) is a separate form placed in the SOURCE-ORDERED compile stream the #55 interleave already builds for BEGIN / use / sub definitions (Parser2 @defs + @def_lines; v1's BEGIN-body path).  Probe: the reproducer, `exists &later` in that BEGIN (perl false), Role-Tiny concrete-methods.t 7/7 and stub.t / role-tiny-with.t staying 4/4, 6/6.
ROWS: Role-Tiny-2.002004-0 concrete-methods.t 1 and 3 (s536b).


=== DONE (s536b) ===
FIXED in the same batch (s536b, commit febff319).  The bodyless `sub NAME;` now emits TWO forms: the section-head stub `(p-declare-sub pl-NAME)` (Pl::Parser::predeclare_sub_form -- the name resolves from the section's start, as before) and the stash entry `(p-declare-sub pl-NAME :forward)` at the declaration's POSITION: Parser2's top level pushes it into @defs with its _src_pos (the #55 source-ordered compile stream, interleaved with BEGIN / use), v1's _process_sub_statement emits it inline (a BEGIN body).  A sub statement inside a block (_lower_named_sub_stmt) keeps the hoisted :forward.  Probe scratch/s536b/p/s2.pl / g4583.pl: tree = perl (BEGIN's own glob aside); Role::Tiny _concrete_methods_of over concrete-methods.t's role (scratch/s536b/p/rt1.pl) = perl.  Guard Pl/t/decl-ordering-02.t row 33, inverse-verified on 0affbe86.  Residue (pre-existing, not changed): `exists &later` written ABOVE the declaration answers true (the head stub sets :stub); perl false.


=== STILL OPEN: the STRING-EVAL half (s536b, ruled by the reviewing session: re-key, do not fix in s536b) ===
Role-Tiny stub.t row 4 ("composing role includes stub subs") still fails on the s536b final tree ff83b7ec (one-file run scratch/s536b/board-tree3.log: 3/4).  Its role is built in a STRING EVAL:

    eval q{ package RoleWithStub; use Role::Tiny; sub stubsub; 1; } or die $@;
    eval q{ package ComposeStub; use Role::Tiny::With; with 'RoleWithStub'; 1; } or die $@;
    ok exists &ComposeStub::stubsub && !defined &ComposeStub::stubsub;   # perl: ok

The FILE-level case matches perl (Pl/t/decl-ordering-02.t row 33, concrete-methods.t 7/7, role-tiny-with.t 6/6), so in an EVAL unit the positional `(p-declare-sub NAME :forward)` evidently still runs BEFORE the `use Role::Tiny` import: Role::Tiny records stubsub as a non-method at import and never composes it.  Suspected site: Pl/Parser2.pm ~2480 (the top-level `sub NAME;` arm that pushes the :forward form into @defs with its _src_pos) -- in eval mode the @defs / sched interleave (or the eval unit's own assembly) may place it ahead of the use's compile-phase form.  Reduce first with a string-eval variant of scratch/s536b/p/g4583.pl (print `keys %P::` from a BEGIN inside the eval string above and below the declaration), then add that row beside decl-ordering-02.t row 33.
ROWS: Role-Tiny-2.002004-0 stub.t 4 (re-keyed from #4561 to #4583 by s536b).
